<title>USA: Harken Energy to drill exploratory wells.</title>
<headline>Harken Energy to drill exploratory wells.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harken Energy Corp said Wednesday it plans to drill three exploratory wells on its Bolivar Association contract at a cost of about $20 million.</p>
<p>Preliminary studies of the 250,000-acre Colombian tract indicate it could hold as much as 30,000 to 100,000 barrels of oil per acre, the company said.</p>
<p>Using horizontal drilling technologies, the tract could yield between 10 percent and 20 percent of the oil in place, or about 3,000 to 20,000 barrels per acre, it said.</p>
</text>
